<title>YEMEN: U.N. to launch projects to help Yemen's poor.</title>
<headline>U.N. to launch projects to help Yemen's poor.</headline>
<dateline>SANAA 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Yemen and the United Nations Development Programme signed an agreement on Thursday to launch projects worth $18 million to help the Arab state fight widespread poverty, state-run radio said.</p>
<p>It gave no further details. UNDP assistance is normally in the form of grants.</p>
<p>Yemen, one of the Middle East's poorest states with per capita income of just $200 a year, launched economic reforms in 1995 in agreement with the World Bank and the International Monetary Fund.</p>
